# Project conventions

## Stack

- Next.js (App Router) with React Server Components, TypeScript in strict mode
- Tailwind CSS v4 (CSS-first config in `src/app/globals.css`, no `tailwind.config`)
- shadcn/ui (Base UI primitives) in `src/components/ui`, icons from `lucide-react`
- Vitest + React Testing Library + jsdom for tests
- Yarn 4 is the only package manager (`node-modules` linker). Never use npm or
  pnpm, and never commit another lockfile.

This Next.js version has breaking changes compared to older releases. Before
using a Next.js API you are not sure about, read the matching guide in
`node_modules/next/dist/docs/`.

## Structure

- `src/app` holds routes only: `page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, `loading.tsx`,
  `error.tsx`, `not-found.tsx`, `route.ts`.
- `src/components` holds feature components; `src/components/ui` is generated
  by shadcn and should only be changed through `yarn dlx shadcn@latest add`.
- `src/lib` holds framework-agnostic helpers and types; `src/hooks` holds
  client hooks.
- Tests sit next to the code they cover as `*.test.ts(x)`.
- Import through the `@/` alias, never with deep relative paths like `../../`.

## Code style

- Components are named function declarations with typed props
  (`type FooProps = { ... }`). One exported component per file.
- Default to Server Components. Add `"use client"` only to the smallest
  component that needs state, effects, or browser APIs.
- Style with Tailwind utilities and merge classes with `cn()`. No inline
  `style` objects, no CSS modules unless asked.
- Prefer semantic HTML and accessible names; every interactive element must be
  usable with a keyboard.
- Handle loading, empty and error states for any data the UI shows.
- No `any`; narrow `unknown` instead. No non-null assertions unless proven.
- Imports are sorted automatically by ESLint; run `yarn lint:fix`.

## Before finishing a change

Run `yarn validate` (typecheck, lint, format check, tests) and fix every failure.
